  "implemented_behavior": "Unit-aware exact arithmetic, bounded polynomial identities and rational-expression domain preservation.",
  "bounded_contract": "Reference checks: id,weight,kind,expected,absolute_tolerance,relative_tolerance. Candidate checks: id,value.\nQuantity profile uses a fixed units whitelist (1,m,cm,mm,km,s,min,kg,g,N,kN,J,kJ,K,degC), canonical dimensions/scales/temperature offsets. Comparison tolerance is max(atol,rtol*abs(expected)) in canonical base units; rtol<=0.01; tolerance is trusted, never supplied by candidate.\nPolynomial profile: exact constant-first coefficient arrays, at most9 entries, trailing zeros normalized. Algebra tolerance must be zero.\nRational-function profile: bounded numerator polynomial, denominator given as product of up to8 factors (x-root), up to16 explicit excluded values; all denominator roots must be excluded. Compare exact cross products and exact domain exclusion sets, so cancellation does not erase a domain hole. No eval or arbitrary expression parser.",
  "bounds_and_open_scope": "Not a general CAS, theorem prover or support for transcendental expressions, arbitrary units, differential equations or unrestricted multivariate algebra. This checks supplied structured work, not extracted equations or mental calculation.",
